  "notes": "PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: prompt says latest Amazon Linux 2 AMI by default but the ground truth hardcodes an AMI id variable default, so no AMI check is written. Region us-east-1 is a provider setting, not visible in plan values, so it is not checked. SSH 'restricted strictly' is enforced positively (a port-22 rule from 10.0.0.0/16) and HTTP/HTTPS must be TCP rules (so an all-protocol 0.0.0.0/0 rule fails); a second, separate port-22 rule from 0.0.0.0/0 cannot be rejected because the interpreter has no negated element match. 'distributed across the private subnets' is checked as instance->subnet refs; per-instance subnet ids are unknown at plan. sg_egress_only_vpc separate-rule branches are not bound to the SG (quantifier all has no ref form); mixing inline and separate egress rules is rare. Name tags (VPC, instances) are detail; the SG name is core because every SG check selects on it."
